source: crates/surfaces/cli/src/main.rs
expression: command.clone().render_long_help().to_string()
---
Create an entity

Usage: specforge new [OPTIONS] [KIND] [ID] [TITLE] [FIELDS]...

Arguments:
  [KIND]
          The kind of entity (behavior, invariant, …)

  [ID]
          The new entity's id

  [TITLE]
          The new entity's title

  [FIELDS]...
          The kind's fields: `--<field> <value>`

Options:
      --in <FILE>
          The file, relative to the spec root; created when missing

      --verify <KIND:TEXT>
          A `verify` obligation, as `kind:text` (or just `text`); repeat for several

      --dry-run
          Print the diff and write nothing

  -h, --help
          Print help (with a kind, that kind's field flags)

      --path <PATH>
          A path inside the project (the nearest directory at or above it holding specforge.json; none: the directory itself, with the default configuration)
          
          [default: .]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format: human or json
          
          [default: human]
          [possible values: human, json]

The kind's fields are flags too: `specforge new <kind> --help` lists them.
